.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt SSH3 1
.Os ssh3-go
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssh3
.Nd SSH3 client: sessions, forwards and file transfers over HTTP/3
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 46AqNvVfM
.Op Fl i Ar identity_file
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl L Ar [bind:]port:host:port
.Op Fl R Ar [bind:]port:host:port
.Op Fl D Ar [bind:]port
.Op Fl J Ar destination
.Op Fl o Ar keyword=value
.Op Fl S Ar ctl_path
.Op Fl -transfer Ar SRC DST
.Ar [user@]host Ns Op :port
.Op Ar command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
connects to an
.Xr ssh3-server 8
endpoint: one QUIC
.Pq UDP
connection carries an HTTP/3 extended CONNECT
.Rs
.%T RFC 9220
.%D October 2022
.Re
to the server route
.Pq default Li /ssh3-term ,
and every subsequent bidirectional stream is an SSH3 channel for
sessions, forwards and file transfers.
The CLI follows the
.Xr ssh 1
canon: the launch keys and the
.Fl o
keywords accept the OpenSSH shapes, the fork's own long names stay
as deprecated aliases; the precedence is CLI flag, then
.Fl o ,
then
.Pa ~/.ssh/config .
.Pp
Authentication: public keys (the OpenSSH agent, the identity files
of the auth plugins; unattended under
.Fl f ) ,
the OIDC id_tokens
.Pq Fl -use-oidc ,
or the classical password prompt
.Pq Fl -use-password .
The first connection pins the server certificate in
.Pa ~/.ssh3/known_hosts
.TofU ,
the
.Fl -strict-host-key-checking
policy
.Pq and the StrictHostKeyChecking -o keyword
governs the pin/ask/refuse decision afterwards.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 4 , Fl 6
Force the IPv4/IPv6 address family for the QUIC dial.
.It Fl i Ar identity_file
The private key file for public key authentication
.Pq the sshd Fl i shape .
.It Fl p Ar port
The remote port, overriding
.Fl o Cm Port ,
the operand port and
.Pa ~/.ssh/config .
.It Fl L Ar [bind:]port:host:port
Local forwarding
.Pq repeatable ;
the
.Cm udp://
prefix marks the documented UDP extension.
.It Fl R Ar [bind:]port:host:port
Reverse forwarding: the server binds and forwards to the local
target
.Pq repeatable .
.It Fl D Ar [bind:]port
Dynamic (SOCKS5) forwarding
.Pq repeatable ;
an empty or
.Cm *
bind listens on every interface.
.It Fl J Ar destination
Proxy jump: a comma-separated chain of SSH3 hops, tunneled UDP hop
by hop
.Pq the Xr ssh 1 Fl J shape .
.It Fl o Ar keyword=value
Configuration option, repeatable: Cm Port, User, IdentityFile,
LocalForward, RemoteForward, DynamicForward, ProxyJump,
ControlMaster, ControlPath, ControlPersist, StrictHostKeyChecking
and the other
.Xr ssh_config 5
keywords the fork implements.
.It Fl M , Fl S Ar ctl_path
Control master mode and its unix socket path (share one connection
across invocations).
.It Fl O Ar op
Control operation on a running master: Cm check, stop, exit.
.It Fl A
Forward the ssh agent to the remote host.
.It Fl f
Go to background after startup: re-execs a detached child after a
non-interactive (key/agent) authentication; interactive
configurations
.Pq passwords, the OIDC browser flow, an unpinned host under the ask policy
refuse up front.
.It Fl N
No remote command or session: hold the connection open for the
forwards.
.It Fl q , Fl v
Quiet / verbose diagnostics.
.It Fl V
Print the software version and exit.
.It Fl -transfer Ar SRC DST
File transfer mode, the scp analog: exactly one operand is
local, the other is
.Ar user@host:path
(upload towards, download from); flags
.Fl r
(recursive),
.Fl -continue
(resume interrupted transfers),
.Fl -checksum
(SHA-256 verification, automatic over 32 MiB).
.It Fl -use-password , Fl -use-oidc , Fl -oidc-config , Fl -no-pkce
The password prompt, the OIDC flow with the issuer URL and its
JSON client config, the PKCE switch.
.It Fl -insecure , Fl -strict-host-key-checking
Certificate verification off; the strict-host-key-checking policy
.Pq Cm yes | no | accept-new | ask .
.It Fl -keylog Ar file
Write the QUIC TLS keys for debugging.
.It Fl -packet-size Ar bytes , Fl -stream-rx-mb Ar mib , Fl -conn-rx-mb Ar mib
QUIC tuning: initial packet size and the flow control receive
windows (defaults 1350, 8, 16).
.It Fl -control-master Cm no | yes | auto , Fl -control-path Ar path , Fl -control-persist Cm no | yes | Ns Ar seconds
The long forms of
.Fl M / Fl S
and the master idle timeout.
.El
.Pp
Deprecated aliases
.Pq the pre-parity fork forms: Fl -privkey , Fl -proxy-jump , Fl -forward-agent , Fl -forward-tcp , Fl -forward-udp , Fl -P , Fl U
stay accepted.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SSH3_LOG_LEVEL
The diagnostic log level
.Pq debug | info | warn | error .
.It Ev SSH3_PPROF
If set, serve the Go pprof endpoint.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/known_hosts
The TOFU pin store of the server certificates.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/config
The OpenSSH configuration, consulted for the implemented keywords.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh3-server 8 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5
